notes.notes:
-This is for a future update, at the moment the release date of said update is within 1-2 weeks as I've been working my actual job and focusing on creating Chapter 2 content.

~For the first 3 story missions enemy stats will be adjusted from 1 to 0.5, and bosses will be adjusted from 1 to 0.75. This means they will deal 50% of current attack power and have 50% of health for normal enemies.

~Credits received for these first 3 story missions will also be reduced by 50%

//This is being done to improve early game content as I was test playing and finding out it is a little bit too difficult. As hunt missions are kind of a way to farm useful subsystems so that the player can gain stat boosts before story missions, they will remain the same. The changes to the first 3 story missions will also make it easier to farm subsystems as well, but while not receiving as many credits. I'll also try and make hunt missions more noticeable within the menu of its capable farming potential.

//Honestly, if it wasn't for a review I would've never really looked into this, so please do reviews or start discussions because they do really help me out on things that I miss or overlook like bugs or possible adjustments. <3

The following changes were made on 1/23/2023:

~Doubled the range on all Tear Drop projectiles as seen in the gif below
[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/42952336/0b77c0522e16734101a6f54ecc42355559fae05a.gif[/img]
//This cannon was always meant to be more of a long range heavy type of weapon, so this buff will really give the cannon more viability now and in the 2nd chapter.

~The level 2 "forward" skill on HonorBound has been changed to a forward moving triple slash
[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/42952336/18bdc34ef8b738c5cc03a8625dfd9e4dda94aa85.gif[/img]
//Most weapons in the 1st chapter were intentionally made to not stand out too much so that they would have a more exact purpose, however HonorBound will be lacking mobility compared to future melee weapons.

~The level 2 "left and right" skills on CQC Type Villain has been changed into an Iframe capable of triggering dusk
[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/42952336/ba0456ea0b186b6d0f3af03fe07ee40d2d481079.gif[/img]
//This weapon had a little bit too much potential in terms of damage, Rage regain due to its multi hits, and mobility on its left and right skills, therefore instead of nerfing it. It's now an iframe with the level 1 skill being slightly buffed.

~Rage meter slowly generates over time at a rate of 1 point per 2 seconds
~Stamina now regains overtime in certain circumstances it previously did not
//In the 2nd chapter there's gonna be these things called titles, (will say more later on lol) either way I chose to make these buffs a thing thats always apparent instead of a buff that needs to be unlocked.

~Mischief's second stage of charging grants a 10% heal
//At the moment as Mischief is the only charge character, my ideas towards this class were kind of limited. But, while working on the 2nd chapter I found a way to make them more interesting. Although, Mischief granting heals seems to fit her better as a general character.

~Collision changes for Dark Serpent and Centipede bosses
